  <h2>Who uses Disclosure-Independent Governance</h2>

  <p>
    Disclosure-Independent Governance is designed for leadership teams and advisors responsible for institutional risk, accountability, workforce visibility, and AI governance.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Boards and board committees</li>
    <li>General Counsel</li>
    <li>Corporate Secretaries</li>
    <li>Chief Risk Officers</li>
    <li>Chief Compliance Officers</li>
    <li>Internal audit leaders</li>
    <li>Human capital and workforce strategy leaders</li>
    <li>CFOs evaluating AI ROI and workforce capacity</li>
    <li>D&amp;O insurance and governance-risk stakeholders</li>
    <li>Executives responsible for AI adoption, vendor oversight, or corporate records</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    The common question is the same:
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    <p>
      Can the organization explain what it relied on, who was accountable, what was measured, what was missed, and what evidence supports the decision?
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <h2 id="published-research-foundations">Published Research Foundations</h2>

  <p>
    Disclosure-Independent Governance is grounded in Lozen Advisory’s published research on Invisible Attrition℠, Tacere, and Disclosure-Independent Performance Protection℠.
  </p>

  <p>
    Akilah E. Kamaria’s SSRN paper, <a href="https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=6397780" rel="noopener noreferrer">“Invisible Attrition℠: A Conceptual Framework for Leadership Capacity Erosion Prior to Organizational Detection”</a>, establishes the workforce-risk foundation for this category: leadership capacity can erode before organizational systems detect loss.
  </p>

  <p>
    The Zenodo preprint, <a href="https://zenodo.org/records/20370916" rel="noopener noreferrer">“Tacere: The Strategic Practice of Non-Disclosure in Professional Environments”</a>, extends that foundation by defining strategic non-disclosure as a governance condition rather than a mere communications, culture, or psychological-safety problem. The record also introduces <a href="/disclosure-independence-infrastructure/"><strong>Disclosure-Independent Performance Protection℠</strong></a> — the individual-facing framework that keeps her professional standing intact and treats her role, her compensation, and her trajectory as assets worth defending, without requiring her to name a condition or crisis before protection can begin — as the individual structural response to Tacere.
  </p>

  <p>
    Together, these published records establish the research basis for Lozen Advisory’s Disclosure-Independent Governance framework: institutions need standards that can evaluate risk without depending on disclosure, visible distress, formal utilization, or after-the-fact detection.
  </p>

